Chapter: CapBlockDenied

 Runtime probe for the widened syscall capability surface: every
 block syscall consults the per-process capability word before
 driving the device. The program declares Device.Block, so the boot
 grant derived from its own manifest includes the block-device bit
 and the first sector count succeeds (0 with no disk attached). It
 then strips its own grant word in the process table and asks again.
 The kernel refuses with -1 without touching the device.

Section: Body

  proc0-cap-addr : Integer = 20536

  strip-grant : Integer -> Integer
  strip-grant (x) =
    let lo = poke-32 proc0-cap-addr 0 0
    in let hi = poke-32 proc0-cap-addr 4 0
    in 0

  opening : [Console, Device.Block] Nothing = act
    before <- block-sector-count
    print-line-uni ("granted: " & show before)
    print-line-uni ("stripped: " & show (strip-grant 0))
    after <- block-sector-count
    print-line-uni ("denied: " & show after)
  end
